<title>USA: U.S. approves $14 billion Boeing merger.</title>
<headline>U.S. approves $14 billion Boeing merger.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Government on Tuesday unconditionally approved the $14 billion merger of Boeing Co. and McDonnell Douglas, helping clear the way for creation of the world's largest aircraft maker.</p>
<p>The Federal Trade Commission approval required no changes to the deal, an FTC spokeswoman said. Attention now turns to Brussels, where the European Union is due to decide this month whether to approve the combination.</p>
</text>
